				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Back: [[Large migrations are more expensive]]]]"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2025-03-31T21:24:53.525+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2025-03-31T21:35:29.753+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "CA6QHAruDQC5HMcHBhk5+g=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "When making a business case for a migration, there can be incentives to underestimate the cost of migrating. People like to work with modern technology, that they don't perceive as being a dead end for their career. The sunk costs effect is real, as soon as a project is started there is loss of face involved in stopping it, and it is often easier to make more time and money available. "
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2025-03-31T21:35:32.828+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2025-03-31T21:38:52.948+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "eAerQgruDQCEh7r3Bhk5+g=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "When a (public) tender is involved, a loose-loose situation is created where there are incentives created to not be transparent about work that needs to be done but is not obvious to one or more of the parties involved."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-19T11:33:17.464093+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-07-19T11:35:10.127684+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "2QvkWjsmQX2WmuTcsClRSw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "###Underestimation\nThe business case for a migration looks better if the costs are lower. So there is always organizational pressure to avoid doing part of the work or to shift costs to other parties. "
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
